{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA update: the recurrence is now narrowed away from generic disk pressure and active JGit autogc. Live /var/gerrit/site/etc/jgit.config has receive.autogc=false and predates the Gerrit process start (file 2026-06-30, Gerrit started 2026-09-07T12:12:48Z), so hypothesis (a) as an active autogc setting is falsified. Full connectivity fsck from both host and in-container gerrit user is clean after repair. The recurring pattern instead involves out-of-process native-git repair/fetches into the live Gerrit repository: the prior repair introduced root-owned pack files at 02:18Z; later JGit receive-pack reported MissingObject for base blob ef9920 even while native git could cat-file it. I normalized object ownership (chown -R 1000:1000 /var/gerrit/site/git/rebar.git/objects) and confirmed container user can read the blob. Prevention change will codify Gerrit's jgit.config and the backup/fetch/fsck/ownership repair protocol in infra so future repairs do not rely on ad-hoc root-owned packs or unversioned host config."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788848814581454001,"uuid":"0a69bb96-6b89-41ab-b866-e0773a689417"}